Advisories (do not block build):
- Stop the `dd` loop on a 0-byte read (EOF / Ctrl+D). Numbered stop conditions list only `\n` and `\r`; a mechanical implementer can busy-loop. `tests/run_tests.sh` times out hung input at 15s.
- On tty submit, write a newline to `/dev/tty`. Cooked `read` echoed Enter; `stty -echo` will not.
- Keep `stty` and the INT/TERM/EXIT trap only in `read_prompt_line` (never inside `$(edit_prompt_line)`). Clear the trap after restore so a sourced test shell does not inherit it.
- Use prefixed locals (`epl_buf`, not `buf`).
- Deinit sites are wired in the same production step as init but have no BS case; rely on the unit editor plus `echo "n" | cmd_deinit --local`.

Radical innovation (advisory, plan left unchanged): drop `edit_prompt_line` as a stdout API. One function, `read_prompt_line`, assigns `rpl_line` (and the same global can be what unit tests assert). That removes the dual contract and the “do not wrap in `$()`” footnote; tty `stty` cannot land in a subshell. Treat 0-byte `dd` as end-of-line in that same function.
